From e01cbf021ae5bed7141e87569ba136f4065dbf5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gareth Davidson <gaz@bitplane.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:57:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Emit relocatable TempleOS modules and raw boot images

Carry AOT options through nested compilation, resolve assembly expressions and symbol imports, and retain initialized code and data with their relocations. Emit raw assembly without executable wrappers or padding, and write complete TempleOS import and termination records.

These changes form the module writer: expression resolution, symbol ownership and relocation output share the same data structures. Native module loading remains available when TempleOS headers redefine the output signature.
